  "interpretation": [
    "CHEBI39010 has no direct molecular-form fields or direct definition in this pinned database. It is a generic MES chemical class under CHEBI38785 morpholines, whose definition is Any compound containing morpholine as part of its structure.",
    "The additional restriction _:riog00799327 is has_role (RO0000087) some CHEBI39011 Good's buffer substance. It is not a has-part assertion, solvent assertion, concentration assertion or equivalence to a prepared buffer stock.",
    "The direct children acid CHEBI39005, anion CHEBI39006 and zwitterion CHEBI39408 all remain distinct classes. Expanded acid/anion/zwitterion restrictions preserve conjugate-acid/base and tautomer relationships rather than identity equality.",
    "The general Good's buffer substance definition mentions zwitterionic buffer substances. The role restriction and that wording do not select zwitterion CHEBI39408 for the JCM bare MES input: the chemical hierarchy includes the acid and anion below the generic MES class.",
    "JCM628 prints MES 0.195 g; JCM629 inherits that immediate input while replacing the carrier. The actual candidates retain the generic CHEBI39010 reference and explicit unknown form. This bounded chemical-class interpretation is supported; acid, anion, zwitterion, sodium salt, buffer-stock preparation, solvent, strength, molecular conversion and supplied-product details are not inferred.",
    "The earlier shorthand compound entity denotes this generic chemical class, not a fully specified single molecular form and not a proof of equality among its members. Absence of a stock assertion alone is not proof that every possible MES product is dry or pure.",
    "Ontology role semantics are described as source facts only. No ingredient role, experiment role, release approval or current whole Mes.yaml owner approval is granted.",
    "Actual selected Mes.yaml CHEBI39010 remains separate from adjacent W07-authored MES acid CHEBI39005. This clarification does not approve the adjacent original source scope or cross-shard union."
  ],
